yoyo changelog, yoyo evolution and yoyo tree now exit 1 when run outside a git repository, instead of printing an error and exiting 0. Committed as 66b1f51a. Build, tests, clippy (-D warnings) and the format check all pass.

Before and after, using the real binary from a fresh `mktemp -d`: before, all three exited 0; now changelog=1 evolution=1 tree=1. The printed text is byte-for-byte the same.

What changed:
• **changelog and evolution:** each now has a version that returns an exit code. The shell commands exit with that code; the REPL's `/changelog` and `/evolution` ignore it and behave as before. This follows how diff/commit/blame were already done.
• **tree:** the function that builds the tree now returns a success or a failure value (`Result`), so the exit code never depends on matching the error text. To keep clippy happy I changed that function's return type instead of keeping two functions, and updated its one test.
• **Two calls I made beyond the task:**
  • "git not installed" also exits 1 for changelog and evolution, since it's the same kind of printed failure. No test covers it.
  • Empty results still exit 0: a repo with no commits, no evolution tags, or no tracked files isn't a failure.

Tests (in tests/integration.rs): one runs the real binary outside a repo and checks for exit 1, the exact output bytes, and nothing on stderr. The other runs all three inside a one-commit temp repo and checks they still exit 0. I also disabled the changelog exit call on purpose: the first test failed by name, and passed again once I restored it.

Docs: the exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists these three, and ARCHITECTURE.md has a new entry under dispatch_sub.rs.

What's left on #982: this is 3 of the 40 return Some(None) arms in dispatch_sub.rs. Known commands that still exit 0 on failure: def/outline when nothing is found, bare run, and tree <bad arg> (the usage message). Whether find/grep with no matches should fail is still undecided. #982 stays open.

I committed only my own files. .yoyo/risk_weights.json was already modified before I started, so I left it uncommitted.
